<title>UK: British election diary - April 24.</title>
<headline>British election diary - April 24.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a list of events in the British election campaign on Thursday -</p>
<p>0830 GMT - LONDON - Prime minister John Major gives daily news conference before setting off on campaign trail.</p>
<p>0915 GMT - LONDON  - Opposition Labour leader Tony Blair gives daily news conference and then campaigns in London.</p>
<p>1330 GMT - LONDON - Labour's shadow chancellor Gordon Brown, national heritage spokesman Jack Cunningham and shadow sports minister Tom Pendry launch party's sports policy.</p>
</text>
